<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yaqui</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yaqui are an Indigenous people of the Yaqui river valley in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonora">Sonora</a>, north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, with communities also in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arizona">Arizona</a>. For centuries they resisted Spanish and then Mexican control of their lands. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porfirio-diaz">Porfirio Díaz</a> they were fought in long campaigns, and thousands were deported to work on plantations in Yucatán.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yaqui.jpg" alt="Yaqui" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Secretaría de Cultura de la Ciudad de México · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yaqui_musicians_2015.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
